{"id": "EUVD-2026-76574", "enisaUuid": "1d9f0fb7-1df2-3719-8567-f73b753a65df", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent lock owner use-after-free during client teardown\n\n__destroy_client() releases a client's open owners, but a lock owner\nwhose only reference is a blocked lock (nbl) stays on\ncl_ownerstr_hashtbl.  client_has_state() does not count a bare owner,\nso DESTROY_CLIENTID can reach __destroy_client() with such owners\npresent.\n\n__destroy_client() then walks the table, calling remove_blocked_locks()\non each owner without a reference.  Freeing a blocked lock drops the\nowner reference held via flc_owner.  The per-net laundromat reaps\nblocked locks from nn->blocked_locks_lru independently of client state.\nThe two paths share blocked_locks_lock only for the list splice, not\nthe owner's lifetime.  The laundromat therefore frees the owner as\n__destroy_client() dereferences it, a NULL dereference in\nremove_blocked_locks().\n\nnfsd4_release_lockowner() holds a reference across the same call;\n__destroy_client() does not.  Hold cl_lock across the walk, taking a\nreference and unhashing each owner, then drop it before\nremove_blocked_locks() and nfs4_put_stateowner(), which take\nblocked_locks_lock and cl_lock.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:33", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42d7954b0a1907d4ef122aef94561952a033cdc3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb38ff8b4dafbbd1781ad37cd96722fdf2cd972a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8bad5a11416b26cc7fd4b18fba46d75ff636558", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ce74d1b7770e69735e8f8e509807af4ff9c8ee7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6ead6fff3a7d03e49845f048f7000a2e0d34431", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4804c58f73a80d12df1de323bf97a164f6ee8743", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8cf4ff0a7c083dd5e0067f517d63979b74b66649", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e2fa29d223a9a1e6a948e40b109d09081d1decd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89662", "GHSA-h9v2-7c48-mpxj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.69, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a917f27-bd7b-303a-9bb6-32b2a479d7ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f44e9da465ea259b6c9f31a627f3c50a16e1679"}, {"id": "14833255-a878-37e4-8ecd-b47a10d26c6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68ef3bc3166468678d5e1fdd216628c35bd1186f <8cf4ff0a7c083dd5e0067f517d63979b74b66649"}, {"id": "292e9237-7416-3c60-ba9a-e89d42cb0ce6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e294c4c2d33b7307a89cdf31bec08a112d6a9297"}, {"id": "2cc2b315-1f43-3480-b9be-1373d1bdad38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.91 <4.10"}, {"id": "2e3b832d-727b-36aa-9424-c36f361799f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.15.14 <4.16"}, {"id": "2eb79b3f-4b2f-3b69-81a1-12c0cf7e0a85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68ef3bc3166468678d5e1fdd216628c35bd1186f <42d7954b0a1907d4ef122aef94561952a033cdc3"}, {"id": "370f609b-07c9-37e6-a67c-8e06a6499699", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68ef3bc3166468678d5e1fdd216628c35bd1186f <1ce74d1b7770e69735e8f8e509807af4ff9c8ee7"}, {"id": "37b4c672-41af-37e3-954d-5fe2dca040b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "39cc5a49-0c49-3cb2-9f6d-dfb0f38469d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "3c62555a-9f0a-3ba0-b766-efe4c0d59fcd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68ef3bc3166468678d5e1fdd216628c35bd1186f <5e2fa29d223a9a1e6a948e40b109d09081d1decd"}, {"id": "4450d88e-